etition constraints and message format. It runs against real Betaflight, which we learned requires at least 1000 sensor samples per second to run real-time correctly.<p>The competition warranted introducing a new feature to generate the camera sensor directly in the simulation loop. Typically people connect to Unreal or similar game engine to create a camera sensor, which works well but is very heavy. For the simple needs of this challenge, creating sample directly in the loop is very handy and easy to use. Happy to hear your feedback on this! While it&#x27;s not fancy looking currently, it uses the Rust Bevy game engine, which should allow us to improve the visual fidelity quickly.<p>We all should easily be able to shift our implementation to the published competition sim once it lands. Hope you enjoy and good luck!", "time": 1779914262, "title": "Show HN: Open-Source AI Racing Harness", "type": "story", "url": "https://www.elodin.systems/post/elodin-ai-grand-prix-race-sim-harness"}, {"by": "root-parent", "descendants": 8, "id": 48297723, "kids": [48303622, 48298722, 48301258, 48300148], "score": 53, "time": 1779903744, "title": "Multi-Agent LLM System for Automated Vulnerability Discovery and Reproduction", "type": "story", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.21779"}, {"by": "arps18", "descendants": 245, "id": 48289950, "kids": [48295884, 48293239, 48294124, 48292593, 48293049, 48291730, 48291572, 48293030, 48291371, 48292040, 48291982, 48290713, 48298177, 48302537, 48297341, 48296144, 48292566, 48292409, 48300674, 48293732, 48292696, 48292225, 48294204, 48292143, 48304272, 48296303, 48296322, 48295078, 48302007, 48291638, 48292386, 48293217, 48296017, 48295963, 48293753, 48292136, 48292195, 48306117, 48302725, 48301803, 48304144, 48291871, 48291867, 48298898, 48303300, 48303369, 48303134, 48292002, 48291997, 48291737, 48290033, 48293469, 48298013, 48296056, 48289951, 48292159, 48290746, 48291682, 48300109, 48291755, 48290714], "score": 412, "time": 1779858819, "title": "Claude Code as a Daily Driver: Claude.md, Skills, Subagents, Plugins, and MCPs", "type": "story", "url": "https://arps18.github.io/posts/claude-code-mastery/"}, {"by": "nathanstitt", "descendants": 33, "id": 48295071, "kids": [48295111, 48300856, 48300757, 48299777, 48297171, 48300951, 48297758, 48297829, 48297811, 48299788, 48297034, 48296308, 48300478, 48307088, 48305589], "score": 102, "time": 1779892601, "title": "Show HN: Open-source Workspace (mail,docs,spreadsheet,drive) web/iOS", "type": "story", "url": "https://tinycld.org/"}, {"by": "singiamtel", "descendants": 11, "id": 48292718, "kids": [48301165, 48302648, 48303402, 48301919, 48307609, 48303255], "score": 80, "time": 1779882049, "title": "Ripgrep AI Policy", "type": "story", "url": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/blob/master/AI_POLICY.md"}, {"by": "delduca", "descendants": 98, "id": 48294791, "kids": [48298240, 48296554, 48296254, 48297097, 48299570, 48305668, 48295897, 48300151, 48296817, 48298621, 48298394, 48296362, 48298175, 48297424, 48296587, 48296892, 48299875, 48296341, 48297334, 48296469, 48296926, 48297969, 48296953, 48305785], "score": 77, "text": "I have a bad memory and can&#x27;t memorize some important numbers, so I created this project.<p>I&#x27;ve always been concerned about being without my phone (getting robbed - which is common in Brazil - running out of battery, having it break, etc.), so I decided to create a page that sends SMS messages (LLM-summarized) and emails with more detailed information such as geolocation, IP address, and the full message.<p>It\u2019s a simple page that allows sending one or more messages, with recipients being myself and other people - for example, in case I or they need help or need to communicate something important.<p>The source code is available at <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;skhaz&#x2F;dokku&#x2F;tree&#x2F;main&#x2F;apps&#x2F;help\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;skhaz&#x2F;dokku&#x2F;tree&#x2F;main&